                    <!-- Q2 -->
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading2">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse2" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse2">
                                Q2. What is the eligibility for CA Foundation 2025/2026?
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div id="faqCollapse2" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading2" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion30">
                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                To appear for CA Foundation, a student must have passed Class 12 (any board, any stream) from a recognised board. Students can also register for CA Foundation after passing Class 10, but they must complete the mandatory 4-month study period before they can appear in the exam. Registration must be done on or before January 1st for the May/June attempt and on or before July 1st for the November/December attempt. There is no age limit, no minimum percentage requirement in Class 12, and no restriction on the number of attempts.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Q3 -->
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading3">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse3" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse3">
                                Q3. How many attempts does CA Foundation have per year?
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div id="faqCollapse3" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading3" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion30">
                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                ICAI conducts CA Foundation exams multiple times a year (including May/June, September, and January). This gives students flexible opportunities to clear the exam. There is no limit on the total number of attempts — students can appear as many times as needed until they clear all four papers. However, clearing in the first attempt saves valuable time and allows students to move to CA Intermediate faster. Excel Educational Institute's coaching program is specifically designed to maximise first-attempt pass rates, which currently stand at 78%+ among our students.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Q4 -->
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading4">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse4" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse4">
                                Q4. Is negative marking in CA Foundation?
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div id="faqCollapse4" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading4" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion30">
                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                Yes, negative marking applies specifically to Papers 3 and 4 of CA Foundation, which are MCQ-based. For every wrong answer, 0.25 marks (one-fourth of a mark) are deducted. There is no negative marking in Papers 1 and 2, which are descriptive/subjective papers. This is why Excel's coaching trains students extensively in elimination strategies for MCQ papers rather than wild guessing. Our mock tests mirror the negative marking pattern so students develop the exact risk-assessment mindset needed to score high in Papers 3 and 4 without losing marks unnecessarily.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Q5 -->
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading5">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse5" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse5">
                                Q5. What is the passing criteria for CA Foundation?
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div id="faqCollapse5" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading5" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion30">
                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                To pass CA Foundation, a student must satisfy two conditions simultaneously. First, they must score at least 40 marks out of 100 (40%) in each individual paper. Second, they must score an aggregate of at least 200 marks out of 400 (50%) across all four papers combined. If a student fails to meet either condition, they do not pass and must re-appear in all four papers in the next attempt. There is no group exemption concept in CA Foundation — all four papers are compulsory in every attempt. Our Excel coaching is structured to ensure students clear both conditions comfortably.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

