                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                ICAI mandates a minimum 4-month study period between CA Foundation registration and appearing in the exam. In practice, most students who join coaching after Class 12 study for 6–8 months before their first attempt. Students who join during Class 11 or early Class 12 have more time and can achieve significantly deeper preparation. At Excel Educational Institute, our standard CA Foundation batch runs for approximately 8–10 months, followed by revision sessions and the Model Test Series before the exam. Students who follow the full Excel program diligently are typically exam-ready well within this period.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Q7 -->
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading7">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse7" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse7">
                                Q7. What subjects are there in CA Foundation?
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div id="faqCollapse7" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading7" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion30">
                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                CA Foundation has four subjects: Paper 1 — Accounting (100 marks, subjective), Paper 2 — Business Laws (100 marks, subjective), Paper 3 — Quantitative Aptitude including Business Mathematics, Logical Reasoning & Statistics (100 marks, objective/MCQ with negative marking), and Paper 4 — Business Economics (100 marks, objective/MCQ with negative marking). The total marks are 400. Each paper must be individually cleared with a minimum of 40 marks, and the aggregate must be at least 200 marks to be declared passed in CA Foundation.
