                                The fee structure at Excel Educational Institute is competitive and transparent, with no hidden charges. Fees vary by batch type — offline, live online, or recorded — and the specific batch timings selected. We offer both full-payment discounts and EMI options for eligible students. Scholarship programs are available for meritorious and economically weaker section students, with discounts up to 100% for Class 12 toppers. To get the current fee structure tailored to your requirements, we recommend calling us, WhatsApping us, or filling the inquiry form on this page.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Q13 -->
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading13">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse13" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse13">
                                Q13. Is hostel facility available for CA Foundation students at Excel?
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div id="faqCollapse13" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading13" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion30">
                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                Yes, Excel Educational Institute has tie-ups with verified, safe, and well-maintained hostels and PG accommodations near our Raipur campus, making it convenient for students coming from Bhilai, Durg, Bilaspur, Dhamtari, Mahasamund, and other cities. The hostels provide furnished rooms (double/triple sharing), home-cooked meals (breakfast, lunch, dinner), 24×7 security with CCTV, high-speed Wi-Fi, and a study-friendly environment. Please contact us specifically for hostel enquiries and we will assist you in finding the best option near the campus.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Q14 -->
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading14">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse14" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse14">
                                Q14. What is the salary of a CA after qualification?
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div id="faqCollapse14" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading14" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion30">
                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                A freshly qualified Chartered Accountant (after clearing CA Final) in India can expect a starting salary ranging from ₹7 to ₹25 LPA depending on the organisation and city. Those placed in the Big 4 accounting firms (Deloitte, EY, PwC, KPMG) typically start at ₹10–25 LPA. CAs joining mid-size firms earn ₹7–12 LPA. CAs in industry roles (as CFO, Finance Manager, or Internal Auditor) in corporate companies earn ₹8–20 LPA. With 5–10 years of experience, a CA's compensation can reach ₹30–60 LPA or more.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Q15 -->
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading15">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse15" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse15">
                                Q15. How is Excel Educational Institute different from other CA coaching in Raipur?
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div id="faqCollapse15" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading15" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion30">
                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                Excel Educational Institute stands apart from other CA coaching institutes in Raipur in several critical ways. First, our entire faculty comprises qualified Chartered Accountants — not commerce graduates or subject matter tutors. Second, our track record of 173+ AIR holders and 16,500+ successful students over 17 years is unmatched in Chhattisgarh. Third, our structured testing cadence, personalised mentorship, Parent App, and multi-mode delivery offer a complete ecosystem. Fourth, our scholarship program ensures that no deserving student is turned away due to financial constraints.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Q16 -->
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading16">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse16" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse16">
                                Q16. Can a Science or Arts student join CA Foundation?
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div id="faqCollapse16" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading16" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion30">
                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                Yes, absolutely. CA Foundation is open to students from all streams — Commerce, Science, and Arts — provided they have passed Class 12. While Commerce students have a head start in Accounting and Business Laws due to prior exposure, Science and Arts students can absolutely succeed in CA Foundation with proper coaching and dedicated effort. At Excel, we have had numerous Science students clear CA Foundation with excellent marks and even secure All India Ranks. Our faculty starts subject teaching from fundamentals.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Q17 -->
                    <div class="accordion-item">
                        <h3 class="accordion-header" id="faqHeading17">
                            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#faqCollapse17" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faqCollapse17">
                                Q17. What is the CA Foundation registration process with ICAI?
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div id="faqCollapse17" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading17" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion30">
                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                To register for CA Foundation with ICAI, visit the ICAI Self-Service Portal (SSP) at eservices.icai.org. Create an account, select "Register for Foundation," fill in personal and educational details, upload scanned documents (Class 10 and 12 mark sheets, identity proof, photograph, and signature), and pay the registration fee online. The current registration fee is approximately ₹9,000. After Class 12 passes, a student must complete a 4-month study period from the date of registration before appearing in the Foundation exam. Our counsellors at Excel provide complete ICAI registration guidance free of charge.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

