                                Q29. What is the difference between CA Foundation, Intermediate, and Final?
                            </button>
                        </h3>
                        <div id="faqCollapse29" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="faqHeading29" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordionRemaining">
                            <div class="accordion-body text-secondary">
                                The CA course consists of three levels:
                                <ol class="mt-2 mb-0">
                                    <li><strong>CA Foundation:</strong> Entry-level exam (4 papers) testing fundamentals of Accounting, Laws, Maths, and Economics.</li>
                                    <li><strong>CA Intermediate:</strong> Second level covering advanced accounting, taxation, auditing, and financial management along with practical articleship training.</li>
                                    <li><strong>CA Final:</strong> Advanced level covering strategic financial reporting, corporate laws, advanced tax, and risk management. Passing CA Final earns the Chartered Accountant designation.</li>
                                </ol>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

